anaging severe gastrointestinal conditions.", "SANGRADO UTERINO:Uterine bleeding is a common cause of iron deficiency anemia, particularly in women.", "ULCUS GASTRODUODENAL:Gastro-duodenal ulcers are sores that develop on the lining of the stomach or the upper part of the small intestine, often causing bleeding.", "HEMORROIDES:Hemorrhoids are swollen veins in the lower rectum and anus that can cause bleeding, contributing to iron deficiency anemia.", "DIVERTICULOSIS:Diverticulosis is a condition characterized by the formation of small pouches in the colon, which can lead to complications such as bleeding and anemia.", "ANGIODISPLASIA:Angiodysplasia is a vascular malformation that can cause gastrointestinal bleeding, contributing to iron deficiency anemia.", "POLIPOSIS:Polyposis refers to the presence of multiple polyps in the gastrointestinal tract, which can lead to bleeding and anemia.", "ACLORHIDRIA:ACLORHIDRIA is a condition characterized by the absence of hydrochloric acid in gastric secretions. This lack of hydrochloric acid can significantly impact the body's ability to absorb iron, potentially leading to deficiencies and related health issues.", "PLUMMER-VINSON SYNDROME:Plummer-Vinson syndrome is a rare condition associated with severe iron deficiency anemia, characterized by esophageal webs and difficulty swallowing.", "HEMOGLOBINA:Hemoglobina is a protein found in red blood cells that plays a crucial role in transporting oxygen throughout the body. It is a key factor in diagnosing anemia, as the levels of hemoglobin are critical indicators of this condition.", "MUCOSAS:Mucosas refer to the mucous membranes in the body, which can be affected by iron deficiency, leading to symptoms like glossitis and angular cheilitis.", "GLANDULAS:Glandulas refer to glands in the body that can be impacted by nutritional deficiencies, including those related to iron."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence